{
  "title": "Platform Modernisation at Northwind Logistics",
  "subtitle": "A fictional sample case study used to test Boku's report layout, charts, diagrams and citations",
  "report_type": "Technology Case Study",
  "executive_summary": [
    "Northwind Logistics, a fictional carrier used here as test data, completed most of a migration of its dispatch platform to Kubernetes by the end of 2025, with 85% of dispatch services running on the new platform [F001]. The programme is best read as a cost and delivery-speed initiative rather than a technology refresh.",
    "Unit infrastructure cost fell from $0.42 to $0.31 per shipment over two years [F002], and deployment frequency rose roughly fourfold [F004]. The deployment figure is derived from company-reported counts and rests on a single source, so it should be treated as indicative.",
    "Management's savings target of about $18 million by 2027 is an estimate made in 2024 [F005]; no later confirmation was found."
  ],
  "key_findings": [
    {
      "headline": "The migration is largely complete",
      "detail": "85% of dispatch services ran on Kubernetes by December 2025 [F001]."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Unit costs fell by about a quarter",
      "detail": "Infrastructure cost per shipment declined from $0.42 in 2023 to $0.31 in 2025 [F002]."
    },
    {
      "headline": "The industry is moving the same way",
      "detail": "61% of surveyed platform teams run production AI inference on Kubernetes [F003]."
    }
  ],
